Copy apply_fixes.sh into the repo root alongside ws_r2_tg30_race_pkg/, then run:

cd /path/to/Outdoor-Racing-Rosmaster-R2-with-tilt-lidar-main
bash apply_fixes.sh

cd ws_r2_tg30_race_pkg
catkin_make
source devel/setup.bash
What the script does internally
It uses two mechanisms:
For modified files (20 files that existed in the original but changed) — it applies a standard unified patch. This means only the actual lines that changed are touched. Everything else in those files is left exactly as the original had it.
For new files (19 files that didn't exist in the original at all — the new Python scripts, racing.rviz, README.md, waypoints.yaml, etc.) — it decodes base64-embedded file content directly. This avoids all heredoc quoting problems with Python single-quotes, backslashes, and special characters.
The script checks you're in the right directory before doing anything, and makes all Python scripts executable at the end.


